<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> BbScannerOptions</h3>
    <pre class="bb-code">BbBarcodeFormat Formats                    = BbBarcodeFormat.All
BbScanRegion    Region                     = BbScanRegion.Full
<span class="k">int</span>           MaxScanLines               = 15      <span class="c">// lines per orientation</span>
<span class="k">int</span>           DownsampleFactor           = 1
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryHarder                  = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// exhaustive detection, full rotation sweep</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          AllowInverted              = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// light on dark symbols</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryReversedRows            = <span class="k">true</span>    <span class="c">// linear symbols read right to left</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryVerticalLines           = <span class="k">true</span>    <span class="c">// columns and tilted lines, for rotated symbols</span>
IReadOnlyCollection&lt;<span class="k">int</span>&gt; ItfLengths      = 6..20 even
<span class="k">bool</span>          Code39CheckDigit           = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// require the modulo 43 check character</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          Code39ExtendedMode         = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// interpret Code 39 as full ASCII</span>
TimeSpan      DuplicateSuppressionWindow = 2 seconds

BbScannerOptions.ForStillImages()   <span class="c">// 60 scan lines, TryHarder, AllowInverted, no suppression</span>
options.Clone()                   <span class="c">// take a copy before editing a running scanner's options</span>
options.Validate()                <span class="c">// throws on an out of range value</span></pre>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        ITF has no check character, so <code>ItfLengths</code> is the main defence against a
        truncated symbol being reported as a shorter, structurally valid number. Narrow it to the
        lengths your application actually uses.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>The decoder</h2>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Headless use</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        The decoding pipeline has no dependency on Blazor or on a browser. It runs anywhere .NET
        runs, which is what makes it testable and benchmarkable.
    </p>
    <pre class="bb-code"><span class="k">using var</span> decoder = <span class="k">new</span> BbBarcodeDecoder(<span class="k">new</span> BbScannerOptions
{
    Formats = BbBarcodeFormat.QrCode | BbBarcodeFormat.DataMatrix,
    DuplicateSuppressionWindow = TimeSpan.Zero,
});

<span class="k">var</span> result = decoder.Decode(rgbaPixels, width, height, BbPixelFormat.Rgba32);
<span class="k">if</span> (result <span class="k">is not null</span>)
{
    Console.WriteLine(<span class="s">$"{result.Format}: {result.Text}"</span>);
    Console.WriteLine(<span class="s">$"took {decoder.LastFrame.Total.TotalMilliseconds:0.00} ms"</span>);
}</pre>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Building blocks</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        Every reader implements <code>IBbRowDecoder</code> for a linear code or
        <code>IBbMatrixDecoder</code> for a two dimensional one, and can be driven directly by a
        pipeline of your own. <code>BbBarcodeDecoder</code> composes the built-in readers from
        <code>Formats</code> and does not accept others.
    </p>
    <pre class="bb-code"><span class="k">public interface</span> IBbRowDecoder
{
    BbBarcodeFormat Formats { <span class="k">get</span>; }
    BbSymbolDecodeResult? DecodeRow(<span class="k">int</span> rowNumber, BbBitRow row, BbBarcodeFormat enabledFormats);
}

<span class="k">public interface</span> IBbMatrixDecoder
{
    BbBarcodeFormat Formats { <span class="k">get</span>; }
    BbSymbolDecodeResult? Decode(BbBitMatrix image, BbMatrixDecodeOptions options);
}</pre>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        Binarisation follows the same shape: <code>IBbBinarizer</code> has one implementation tuned for
        matrix codes, one for linear rows and a global histogram fallback, each usable on its own.
    </p>
</div>
